# An argument of a method of a native generic type is checked against what the
# instance takes for the type's parameter. The methods of such a type are
# shared by its instances and keep the parameter in their signature, so the
# argument used to go unchecked: the C compiler was the first to object.

main: function is {
    m: (sync.MutexVal i64).create value: "x"
    a: (sync.Atomic i64).create value: "x"
    l: (sync.Mutex (ListVal i64)).create value: 5
    print "a"
}
